00:00:07.639 --> 00:00:09.440 align:start position:0%
25 years ago the United Nations  established an international scientific  body known as the Intergovernmental  Panel on Climate Change or IPCC it's job  is to provide world leaders with the  best available information about how  climate is changing and what could be  done about the problem the IPCC has  issued reports about every six years and  a scientific understanding of the issue  has grown so has the size of the reports  and the number of experts involved in  producing them to make forecasts about  how quickly the globe will warm and how  the pattern will vary by region  researchers use computer climate models  that simulate the various elements of  the Earth's atmosphere and oceans the  resolution of those models has improved  by a factor of 10 over the past 25 years  allowing for much more refined  projections of how the climate will warm  researchers are now good at modeling the  current climate but they're still not  sure how sensitive the earth will be to  rising atmospheric concentrations of  greenhouse gases like carbon dioxide in  fact the estimates of such climate  sensitivity have not changed much in 25  years  but the IPCC has grown much more  confident over time that humans are  causing the bulk of the recent warming  and that without major reductions in  pollution from fossil fuels earth's  temperature will continue to rise check  out nature calm for the full story
 

